@@ -0,0 +1,220 @@
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch document structure is validated
+Per RFC 6902 §3, a patch SHALL be an array of operation objects, each with a string `op` member naming one of
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`. Members other than those defined for the operation SHALL be
+ignored. Invalid patches SHALL be rejected with an error before the document is changed (§5).
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, `null`, or a string
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** the result equals the document
+
+#### Scenario: Operation is not an object, or `op` missing, not a string, or unknown
+- **WHEN** an operation is `null`, `[]`, `{"path":"/a"}`, `{"op":1,"path":""}` or `{"op":"nop","path":""}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Required members missing or of wrong type
+- **WHEN** `path` is missing or not a string, `value` is missing for `add`/`replace`/`test`, or `from` is missing or not a string for `move`/`copy`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown extra members are ignored
+- **WHEN** an operation is `{"op":"remove","path":"/a","comment":"x"}`
+- **THEN** the operation is applied normally
+
+#### Scenario: `value` may be null
+- **WHEN** the operation is `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}`
+- **THEN** member `a` is set to `null`
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid pointer
+- **WHEN** `path` or `from` is not a valid RFC 6901 pointer, e.g. `"a"` or `"/a~2"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Operations apply sequentially and atomically
+Per RFC 6902 §3 and §5, operations SHALL be applied in order, each to the result of the previous one. If any
+operation fails, an error SHALL be thrown and no partial result returned.
+
+#### Scenario: Sequential application
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":1},{"op":"replace","path":"/a","value":2}]` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Later failure
+- **WHEN** the first operation succeeds and the second fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the input document is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: Input is never mutated
+`applyPatch` SHALL NOT mutate the document or the patch, and the result SHALL NOT share object or array
+references with the document or with the patch's `value` members.
+
+#### Scenario: Document unchanged
+- **WHEN** any patch is applied to a document
+- **THEN** the document deep-equals its prior copy afterwards
+
+#### Scenario: Values from the patch are copied
+- **WHEN** an `add` inserts an object `value` and the result is then modified
+- **THEN** the patch's `value` is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch returns a new value
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]` and the document is an object
+- **THEN** the result is not the same reference as the document
+
+### Requirement: add
+Per RFC 6902 §4.1, `add` SHALL, for an object parent, set the member (replacing an existing one); for an array
+parent, insert before the given index, shifting later elements; with the index `-`, append; with the empty path,
+replace the whole document. The parent SHALL exist; an array index SHALL be a valid index no greater than the
+array length.
+
+#### Scenario: Add a new object member
+- **WHEN** `add` `/b` value `2` on `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1,"b":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces an existing member
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a` value `2` on `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add into array inserts
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/1` value `"x"` on `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","x","q"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add at array end
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/-` value `"x"`, or `/a/2`, on `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** `"x"` is appended
+
+#### Scenario: Add beyond array end or with invalid index
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/3` on a 2-element array, or `/a/01`, `/a/-1`, `/a/x`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add with missing parent
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/b` on `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add to a scalar parent
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/b` on `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces the whole document
+- **WHEN** `add` with path `""` value `[1]` on `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `[1]`
+
+#### Scenario: Empty-string member name
+- **WHEN** `add` `/` value `1` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Escaped member names
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a~1b` value `1` and `/m~0n` value `2` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a/b":1,"m~n":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Hostile key
+- **WHEN** `add` `/__proto__` value `{"x":1}` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member `__proto__`, `Object.prototype` is unaffected, and `({}).x` is `undefined`
+
+### Requirement: remove
+Per RFC 6902 §4.2, `remove` SHALL delete the target, which MUST exist. Removing an array element shifts later
+elements down. Removing the whole document (empty path) would leave no JSON value, so it SHALL be rejected with an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove an object member
+- **WHEN** `remove` `/a` on `{"a":1,"b":2}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove an array element
+- **WHEN** `remove` `/a/0` on `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["q"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove the whole document
+- **WHEN** `remove` path `""`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Remove a missing target
+- **WHEN** `remove` `/x` on `{}`, `/a/5` on a 2-element array, or `/a/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace
+Per RFC 6902 §4.3, `replace` SHALL replace the value at the target, which MUST exist. It is equivalent to
+`remove` followed by `add`.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace a member or element
+- **WHEN** `replace` `/a` value `2` on `{"a":1}`, or `/a/0` on `{"a":[1]}`
+- **THEN** the value is replaced and array length is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Replace a missing target
+- **WHEN** `replace` `/b` on `{"a":1}`, or `/a/1` on a 1-element array
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace the whole document
+- **WHEN** `replace` path `""` value `5`
+- **THEN** the result is `5`
+
+### Requirement: move
+Per RFC 6902 §4.4, `move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path`, as `remove`
+followed by `add`. `from` MUST NOT be a proper prefix of `path`.
+
+#### Scenario: Move an object member
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a` to `/b` on `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move within an array
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a/0` to `/a/2` on `{"a":["p","q","r"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["q","r","p"]}` (add applies after removal)
+
+#### Scenario: Move to the same location
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and exists
+- **THEN** the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a` to `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move from a missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy
+Per RFC 6902 §4.5, `copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from` (which MUST exist) at `path`.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy a value
+- **WHEN** `copy` from `/a` to `/b` on `{"a":{"x":1}}`, then `/b/x` is replaced with `2`
+- **THEN** `/a/x` is still `1`
+
+#### Scenario: Copy from a missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test
+Per RFC 6902 §4.6, `test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) equals `value`, and
+otherwise an error SHALL be thrown. Equality follows §4.6: strings by code points, numbers by numeric value,
+arrays by length and element equality in order, objects by equal member sets with equal values regardless of
+order, and literals by identity.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal values
+- **WHEN** `test` `/a` value `{"x":[1,2],"y":null}` and the document has `{"a":{"y":null,"x":[1,2]}}`
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds and the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Different values or types
+- **WHEN** the values are `1` vs `"1"`, `0` vs `false`, `null` vs missing, `[1,2]` vs `[2,1]`, or objects with different member sets
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Numbers compare by value
+- **WHEN** `test` value `1.0` against `1`
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown, even when `value` is `null`
+
+#### Scenario: Test aborts the patch
+- **WHEN** a `test` fails in the middle of a patch
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and later operations do not take effect
+
+#### Scenario: Test of the whole document
+- **WHEN** `test` path `""` value equals the document
+- **THEN** the patch succeeds
+
+### Requirement: Errors are identifiable
+All errors raised for an invalid patch or failed operation SHALL be instances of `JsonPatchError`, which extends `Error`.
+
+#### Scenario: Error class
+- **WHEN** any invalid patch or failed operation occurs
+- **THEN** the thrown error is an instance of `JsonPatchError` and of `Error`
